          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• The egg of a hummingbird typically is 1.3 cm long and 0.9 cm wide."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.112,
            0.847,
            0.151
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The Philippine Goby is about 0.9 cm long. It can be found in the Philippines and other Southeast Asian countries."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.154,
            0.848,
            0.211
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The smallest known jellyfish, Irukandji, has a belly size of 0.5 – 2.5 cm. Its tentacles can be as long as 1 m. They are found in Australia. Its venom can be fatal to humans."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.216,
            0.848,
            0.291
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The Wolfi octopus, also known as the Star-sucker Pygmy Octopus, is the smallest known octopus in the world. Their typical size is around 1 – 2.5 cm and they weigh less than 1 gm. They are found in the Pacific Ocean."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.308,
            0.39,
            0.33
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Weight Conversion"
